+      "message": "STATE.md next_action names , claimed by  while this state's agent is  -- executing another agent's claim is the concurrency collision В§ 1.4 exists to prevent",
       "disposition": "INTENTIONALLY_NO_MUTATION_CASE",
       "reason": "The condition spans two files at one instant: STATE.md carries the pre-computed pick and BOARD.md carries the claim fields, while a CASES entry mutates exactly one file (audit_checks.case_target resolves to root/rel). A BOARD-only mutation can make the claim live but leaves the pick naming a different ticket, and a STATE-only mutation can repoint the pick but cannot make some ticket's claim live -- so the sweep would go red on the Pick-Rule or claim-format checks and prove nothing about this one. What proves the invariant instead: tools/test_t1598_stale_claim_next_action.py builds a whole project and drives this exact check red on a FOREIGN_LIVE claim and on an INVALID half pair, and green on a FOREIGN_STALE one."
     },
